# What NOT to upload to Cloud Build.
#
# `gcloud run deploy --source .` tars the working directory. Without this it
# would ship target/ — tens of gigabytes of build output — on every deploy,
# which is slow enough to look like a hang.
.git/
.gitnexus/
target/
dist/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
*.dmg
*.gz

# The provisioning Dockerfile copies only Cargo metadata, crates/, deploy/,
# src/, root markdown, and docs/. Keeping unrelated demos, app assets, SDKs,
# test goldens, and repository automation out of the upload cuts the build
# context by roughly 180 MiB without changing the image input.
.cargo/
.claude/
.github/
.jcode/
assets/
changelog/
ios/
scripts/
sdk/
telemetry-worker/
tests/
score_shard.py

# Scratch screenshots accidentally left under a crate must never become build
# context merely because the containing crate is required.
crates/**/.tmp/
